{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/hu7vut","slideIndex":1,"text":"[0:15–0:45] Cardiac development is difficult because students usually see separate textbook stages. They must imagine the movement between them, then connect a developmental change to the congenital anatomy that appears later. Congenital heart defects affect about one in one hundred births, so understanding that process matters. HeartV0 makes the sequence visible and manipulable.\n\nSource: Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, About Congenital Heart Defects, https://www.cdc.gov/heart-defects/about/index.html"}
