{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/iaquh5","slideIndex":3,"text":"[1:15–1:55] The current build is much more complete than my earlier prototype. It now contains fifty-two guided cards across ten developmental and six anomaly lessons, plus eight exploration stops and sixteen teaching assets. Important transitions can now morph rather than only switching between static stages. Learners can inspect layers, compare later anatomy and follow links between normal development and related anomalies. Some intervals still use stage snapshots, so I describe this as key transition morphing rather than one continuous animation.\n\nInternal source: Documentation/RESEARCH_ITERATION.md and current October 28 build verification."}
