{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/8wo17i","slideIndex":4,"text":"[1:55–2:30] My course journey was iterative rather than linear. I started by learning an unfamiliar spatial platform and proving that I could place and manipulate the anatomy. Then I had to connect the technical build to an actual learning sequence. Testing exposed clutter, unclear controls and gaps between development and clinical anatomy. Each round of evidence changed the next design decision. The main lesson was that innovation came from repeated making, questioning and improving."}
